# Accounts the IONIS units run as. systemd-sysusers creates them at install, so the timers
# have an account to run as on ANY host — including a stranger's, installing from Copr.
# Before 4.0.8 the units named `ki7mt`, a human account that exists only on this lab's
# control node, so they could not start anywhere else.
#
# IDS ARE ALLOCATED AUTOMATICALLY ("-"), as sysusers.d(5) recommends unless a specific id is
# strictly necessary. It is not necessary for correctness here, and a public package has no
# business claiming 970/971 on someone else's system.
#
# This lab DOES pin them (ionis-data 970, ionis-ingest 971) because its data is backed up and
# replicated between hosts, where a differing uid turns a restore into a chown hunt — but it
# pins them in fleet-ops/ionis-service-accounts.yml, which runs first. sysusers leaves an
# existing account alone, so the lab keeps its fixed ids and everyone else gets a free one.
g ionis-data   -
u ionis-ingest -:ionis-data "IONIS ingest pipelines" /var/lib/ionis-ingest /sbin/nologin
